1
00:00:25,926 --> 00:00:28,160
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,303
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,416 --> 00:00:51,450
♪ ♪

4
00:01:27,054 --> 00:01:29,221
♪ ♪

5
00:01:55,716 --> 00:01:58,784
Forgive me, Father,
for I have sinned.

6
00:01:58,852 --> 00:02:02,721
It's been three weeks
since my last confession.

7
00:02:04,891 --> 00:02:06,825
♪ ♪

8
00:02:36,390 --> 00:02:38,624
Will you come back here? No!

9
00:02:38,692 --> 00:02:40,792
You're worse than he is!

10
00:02:56,544 --> 00:03:00,244
My two boys were born
here at St. Ignatius Hospital.

11
00:03:00,314 --> 00:03:03,247
I never forgot
that, or this church.

12
00:03:03,317 --> 00:03:07,352
Anyway... I got a
lot to be grateful for,

13
00:03:07,421 --> 00:03:09,888
and that's why I'm
donating this brand-new wing

14
00:03:09,957 --> 00:03:11,323
to St. Ignatius.

15
00:03:16,197 --> 00:03:20,799
So I could sort of pay back
everybody I owe, all at once.

16
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:25,103
The City of Atlanta,
the people of Atlanta,

17
00:03:25,172 --> 00:03:28,106
and, of course, the
good Lord above.

18
00:03:28,175 --> 00:03:30,008
He doesn't want it!

19
00:03:30,077 --> 00:03:31,810
The Almighty Father has no use

20
00:03:31,879 --> 00:03:34,679
for something that was
built in the spirit of deceit.

21
00:03:34,748 --> 00:03:37,260
Father Fitzgerald... Oh,
God knows who you are,

22
00:03:37,284 --> 00:03:40,151
what you are and what
you're doing here, Mr. Carlino!

23
00:03:40,221 --> 00:03:42,820
Father... He doesn't want any
false acts of charity from you.

24
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:45,201
Father, don't. Now,
everybody, please, go home.

25
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:46,858
There'll be no ceremony here.

26
00:03:46,927 --> 00:03:48,493
What the hell's going on here?

27
00:03:48,562 --> 00:03:49,873
You know very well. Father...

28
00:03:49,897 --> 00:03:51,095
You should be ashamed!

29
00:03:51,165 --> 00:03:53,331
Of what? Why is
he doing this to me?

30
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,345
Go home, Father.
Hey, wait a minute.

31
00:03:55,369 --> 00:03:56,568
He can't just walk away.

32
00:03:56,637 --> 00:03:58,348
I don't know what
he's talking about.

33
00:03:58,372 --> 00:03:59,971
I'm talking about corruption,

34
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:01,372
I'm talking about graft,

35
00:04:01,441 --> 00:04:03,875
I'm talking about the way
your construction company

36
00:04:03,944 --> 00:04:05,911
built this wing of our hospital!

37
00:04:05,979 --> 00:04:07,624
Not here, Father, please!

38
00:04:07,648 --> 00:04:08,991
I don't care if
you are a priest,

39
00:04:09,015 --> 00:04:10,360
you better be
able to back it up.

40
00:04:14,722 --> 00:04:17,282
Oh, I'm so sorry,
Your Excellency.

41
00:04:17,324 --> 00:04:19,736
I shouldn't have made
those accusations public...

42
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,292
You're right.

43
00:04:21,361 --> 00:04:24,874
Well, there'll be a full report
on your desk in the morning.

44
00:04:24,898 --> 00:04:26,178
Thank you.

45
00:04:26,233 --> 00:04:27,510
Good-bye.

46
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:33,004
I know who made the phone call

47
00:04:33,073 --> 00:04:35,840
to the archbishop about
the incident this morning.

48
00:04:35,909 --> 00:04:36,909
You do?

49
00:04:36,977 --> 00:04:39,210
Don't play the
innocent with me, Paul.

50
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,645
It doesn't suit you.

51
00:04:40,714 --> 00:04:43,226
Father, you don't
seriously... Please,

52
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:45,650
don't insult my intelligence.

53
00:04:45,719 --> 00:04:49,254
If you don't mind,
I'd like to be alone.

54
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:22,353
Father Fitzgerald?

55
00:05:26,226 --> 00:05:28,159
What happened?

56
00:05:28,228 --> 00:05:30,195
I don't know.

57
00:05:30,264 --> 00:05:32,697
Someone must have come in here,

58
00:05:32,766 --> 00:05:36,067
tore it off the wall and
deliberately destroyed it.

59
00:05:38,271 --> 00:05:40,204
Who would've done that?

60
00:05:40,273 --> 00:05:41,940
That's a sacrilege.

61
00:05:42,009 --> 00:05:43,774
Yes, it is.

62
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,500
Night, Mrs. Curtis.

63
00:06:08,569 --> 00:06:11,202
Oh, night, Mr. Bell.

64
00:06:11,271 --> 00:06:13,138
You're working late yourself.

65
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:16,374
It doesn't get any
easier around here.

66
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,913
What in the world was that?

67
00:06:21,982 --> 00:06:23,748
Stay here.

68
00:07:26,412 --> 00:07:28,880
He's dead.

69
00:07:28,949 --> 00:07:31,482
What did he say?

70
00:07:31,552 --> 00:07:33,351
What, are you crazy?

71
00:07:33,419 --> 00:07:35,219
I didn't kill this priest.

72
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:37,266
Funny, that's not what he said.

73
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:40,892
I don't care what he
said... I didn't do it.

74
00:07:40,961 --> 00:07:43,594
Mr. Carlino, we've got a
statement from a dying man,

75
00:07:43,663 --> 00:07:46,398
and the dying man
happens to be a priest.

76
00:07:46,467 --> 00:07:49,935
Well, either he was a
liar or he was mistaken

77
00:07:50,003 --> 00:07:51,602
or he is nuts.

78
00:07:51,671 --> 00:07:53,771
I did not do it.

79
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:56,641
You sure you can't prove where
you were between 9:00 and 10:00?

80
00:07:56,710 --> 00:07:58,643
I already told you.

81
00:07:58,712 --> 00:08:00,423
I was home... Yeah.

82
00:08:00,447 --> 00:08:03,014
Alone.

83
00:08:06,119 --> 00:08:08,052
Mm-hmm.

84
00:08:10,256 --> 00:08:12,223
Eh, what's that?

85
00:08:12,292 --> 00:08:14,358
It's a time and
labor-saving device.

86
00:08:14,427 --> 00:08:16,393
We call it a confession.

87
00:08:16,463 --> 00:08:17,662
I want my attorney.

88
00:08:17,730 --> 00:08:18,930
I'm not signing this.

89
00:08:18,999 --> 00:08:20,959
I shouldn't even
be talking to you.

90
00:08:22,836 --> 00:08:24,935
Let me save you some legal fees.

91
00:08:25,004 --> 00:08:27,438
We just got a statement
from an eyewitness

92
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:31,108
that you saw running
away from the house.

93
00:08:33,479 --> 00:08:34,779
What kind of a frame is this?

94
00:08:34,848 --> 00:08:37,314
I wouldn't say anything
else, Mr. Carlino.

95
00:08:37,384 --> 00:08:39,183
Who are you?

96
00:08:39,253 --> 00:08:41,853
I'm Alex Winthrop.

97
00:08:41,922 --> 00:08:43,888
I'm your attorney.

98
00:08:43,957 --> 00:08:46,324
You're my attorney?

99
00:08:46,393 --> 00:08:47,525
Yes.

100
00:08:47,594 --> 00:08:49,405
I'd like to speak to
my client privately.

101
00:08:49,429 --> 00:08:50,862
Sure.

102
00:08:50,930 --> 00:08:52,497
Let's go.

103
00:08:52,566 --> 00:08:55,767
Lieutenant... you
can take this with you.

104
00:08:55,835 --> 00:08:57,435
I don't think we'll
be needing it.

105
00:08:57,503 --> 00:09:00,063
Well, I'll keep it
handy, just in case.

106
00:09:03,009 --> 00:09:04,976
I'm sorry I'm late.

107
00:09:05,045 --> 00:09:07,222
I, uh, I got the first
flight out of New York,

108
00:09:07,246 --> 00:09:09,680
and then the airline
lost my luggage.

109
00:09:09,750 --> 00:09:11,116
And, uh, I couldn't get a cab.

110
00:09:11,184 --> 00:09:12,349
You know how that goes.

111
00:09:12,419 --> 00:09:14,452
Look, Al, uh... Alex.

112
00:09:14,521 --> 00:09:16,221
I'm in serious trouble here.

113
00:09:16,289 --> 00:09:18,223
Yes.

114
00:09:18,291 --> 00:09:19,891
I know.

115
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,804
I spoke to the
arresting officer.

116
00:09:21,828 --> 00:09:25,262
My family pays, uh, Benson,
Reese, Cline and Dunhill

117
00:09:25,332 --> 00:09:28,265
a small fortune each
year in legal fees.

118
00:09:28,335 --> 00:09:31,435
I was hoping they'd send
me a top defense attorney.

119
00:09:33,006 --> 00:09:34,973
I don't know how to say this...

120
00:09:35,041 --> 00:09:37,575
A guy with some
gray in his hair.

121
00:09:37,644 --> 00:09:40,745
I'm only here to make a
preliminary assessment.

122
00:09:40,814 --> 00:09:43,848
I'm gonna get you a top
man as my co-counsel.

123
00:09:43,917 --> 00:09:45,449
Yeah?

124
00:09:45,518 --> 00:09:46,518
Who's that?

125
00:09:50,089 --> 00:09:52,524
Hey, Ray Weid!
Nice-looking suit.

126
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:54,526
Hey.

127
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:56,071
Man must be colorblind. Hey!

128
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:57,695
Ben. Huh?

129
00:09:57,764 --> 00:09:59,697
Hey! Alex!

130
00:09:59,766 --> 00:10:01,533
Hey! God!

131
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:02,601
How are ya?

132
00:10:02,636 --> 00:10:03,713
I feel great!

133
00:10:03,737 --> 00:10:04,747
You look great, too.

134
00:10:04,771 --> 00:10:06,011
Well, I guess we're both great.

135
00:10:06,072 --> 00:10:07,282
Yeah! Were you in the courtroom?

136
00:10:07,306 --> 00:10:08,350
Yeah, oh, yeah.

137
00:10:08,374 --> 00:10:09,785
I love watching
you play the jury.

138
00:10:09,809 --> 00:10:11,453
It's like Itzhak Perlman
with Stradivarius.

139
00:10:11,477 --> 00:10:13,745
Well, talk like that'll
get you a free hot dog.

140
00:10:13,813 --> 00:10:15,546
Come on. I'm game. I'm game.

141
00:10:15,616 --> 00:10:17,416
What are you doing in town?

142
00:10:17,451 --> 00:10:20,385
Well, Ben, I've got
my first real case.

143
00:10:20,454 --> 00:10:22,387
Well, congratulations!

144
00:10:22,456 --> 00:10:23,721
Thank you.

145
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:25,090
Thank you very much.

146
00:10:25,158 --> 00:10:26,924
Actually, I'm, uh,

147
00:10:26,993 --> 00:10:28,304
I'm a little nervous about it.

148
00:10:28,328 --> 00:10:29,394
Nervous, huh?

149
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:30,463
Hey, Charlie, two dogs.

150
00:10:30,497 --> 00:10:32,163
Two dogs.

151
00:10:32,232 --> 00:10:35,166
So, um, you're pretty busy.

152
00:10:35,235 --> 00:10:36,834
Yeah, pretty busy.

153
00:10:36,903 --> 00:10:38,836
Pretty busy.

154
00:10:38,905 --> 00:10:40,115
Here. I-I got... I'll get it.

155
00:10:40,139 --> 00:10:41,551
I'll get it. I'll get it. Oh.

156
00:10:41,575 --> 00:10:42,585
Keep it.

157
00:10:42,609 --> 00:10:44,375
All right.

158
00:10:44,444 --> 00:10:46,378
Hey.

159
00:10:48,548 --> 00:10:50,482
Hey, you're a
pretty big spender.

160
00:10:50,550 --> 00:10:52,428
Well... hell, I like you.

161
00:10:52,452 --> 00:10:54,697
I mean, a man of your
stature deserves the very best.

162
00:10:54,721 --> 00:10:56,688
You gave him $20.

163
00:10:57,791 --> 00:11:00,725
Yeah, like I said,
you deserve the best.

164
00:11:00,794 --> 00:11:04,062
You can get a hot
dog with everything,

165
00:11:04,130 --> 00:11:08,566
including bacon and
avocado, for $3.20.

166
00:11:08,635 --> 00:11:12,069
And if you want a whole plate
of French fries and pickles,

167
00:11:12,139 --> 00:11:15,973
some places, that's
$1.50, $2.00 tops.

168
00:11:16,042 --> 00:11:19,009
So now you're up
to $5.20 apiece.

169
00:11:19,079 --> 00:11:20,678
And if you want a bottle of pop,

170
00:11:20,746 --> 00:11:23,214
a cup of coffee...
Stretch it 75 cents.

171
00:11:23,283 --> 00:11:26,884
So now-now-now
you're at, uh, $5.95.

172
00:11:26,953 --> 00:11:29,486
You gave him a 20 spot.

173
00:11:29,556 --> 00:11:31,489
Yeah, well, I...

174
00:11:31,558 --> 00:11:33,424
I guess it was kind of dumb.

175
00:11:33,493 --> 00:11:35,326
Yeah.

176
00:11:35,395 --> 00:11:37,929
Can I ask you something?

177
00:11:37,997 --> 00:11:41,465
Man buys me a $20 hot
dog... Ask me anything.

178
00:11:41,535 --> 00:11:44,768
This case that I have
that I'm nervous about...

179
00:11:44,837 --> 00:11:46,937
Yeah?

180
00:11:47,007 --> 00:11:48,539
Will you be my co-counsel?

181
00:11:48,608 --> 00:11:49,774
Co-counsel?

182
00:11:49,843 --> 00:11:51,575
You'd be very well paid.

183
00:11:51,644 --> 00:11:52,644
Police report.

184
00:11:52,679 --> 00:11:54,378
Criminal case?

185
00:11:54,448 --> 00:11:55,646
Murder.

186
00:11:59,219 --> 00:12:01,919
Oh, Alex.

187
00:12:01,988 --> 00:12:03,020
You got trouble.

188
00:12:05,825 --> 00:12:07,291
Yeah, I know.

189
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:10,294
You better buy me
another $20 hot dog.

190
00:12:21,441 --> 00:12:25,043
Bail is set at $250,000.

191
00:12:25,111 --> 00:12:27,045
Court will take a
15 minute recess.

192
00:12:31,451 --> 00:12:35,553
Mr. Matlock, I can't tell you
how glad I am you're on my case.

193
00:12:35,621 --> 00:12:36,921
I've read a lot about you.

194
00:12:36,990 --> 00:12:39,757
I've read a lot about you, too.

195
00:12:39,826 --> 00:12:42,960
Don't confuse me with
the rest of my family.

196
00:12:43,029 --> 00:12:45,796
I run a totally legitimate
operation here.

197
00:12:45,866 --> 00:12:48,433
How about that
one in New Jersey,

198
00:12:48,501 --> 00:12:51,569
where you were arrested
for trying to bribe a city official

199
00:12:51,638 --> 00:12:53,204
for criminal negligence?

200
00:12:53,273 --> 00:12:55,339
Yeah, but I walked.

201
00:12:55,408 --> 00:13:00,277
Getting off on a mistrial is
not the same as acquittal.

202
00:13:02,048 --> 00:13:05,283
Look, I never said I didn't
make a few mistakes.

203
00:13:05,352 --> 00:13:07,432
I was young, kind of
hotheaded, you know.

204
00:13:08,722 --> 00:13:11,589
But I was always smart
enough to get a good lawyer.

205
00:13:11,657 --> 00:13:14,092
So when Alex here said
he was gonna get you,

206
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:15,593
I knew I was in good hands.

207
00:13:15,662 --> 00:13:19,363
Let me get something
straight here.

208
00:13:19,432 --> 00:13:21,465
The only reason I'm on this case

209
00:13:21,534 --> 00:13:25,336
is because of my
friendship with Mr. Winthrop.

210
00:13:25,404 --> 00:13:27,672
To tell you the truth,
I-I don't hold out

211
00:13:27,741 --> 00:13:29,674
a hell of a lot of hope for you.

212
00:13:29,743 --> 00:13:31,943
We'll give it our best shot.

213
00:13:32,012 --> 00:13:34,545
After you're released, I want
you to go home, stay there,

214
00:13:34,614 --> 00:13:36,525
keep your mouth shut.

215
00:13:36,549 --> 00:13:39,109
Don't get even as
much as a traffic ticket

216
00:13:39,152 --> 00:13:40,563
till this trial is over.

217
00:13:40,587 --> 00:13:42,019
You got that?

218
00:13:42,088 --> 00:13:44,255
Yeah, I got that.

219
00:13:44,324 --> 00:13:45,923
I'll be home if you need me.

220
00:13:53,199 --> 00:13:55,633
I been a Catholic all my life.

221
00:13:55,701 --> 00:13:58,602
There's no way
I'd kill a priest.

222
00:13:58,672 --> 00:14:00,071
Hm.

223
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:08,846
So you told him you'd get me.

224
00:14:08,915 --> 00:14:10,748
Well, yeah.

225
00:14:10,816 --> 00:14:14,285
I thought you might, if I, um...

226
00:14:14,354 --> 00:14:16,721
Traded on our relationship?

227
00:14:16,790 --> 00:14:19,624
Well, yes.

228
00:14:19,693 --> 00:14:23,594
Well, that's one way to do it.

229
00:14:26,666 --> 00:14:29,700
Alex, you may have a
place in this business.

230
00:14:29,769 --> 00:14:31,368
So do you think he did it?

231
00:14:33,473 --> 00:14:35,306
Beats me.

232
00:14:35,374 --> 00:14:37,875
I'm not Catholic.

233
00:14:37,944 --> 00:14:39,977
But from what I've heard,

234
00:14:40,046 --> 00:14:43,414
it would be real hard for
one of them to kill a priest.

235
00:14:45,518 --> 00:14:47,351
Yeah.

236
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:48,353
Yeah.

237
00:14:48,421 --> 00:14:49,665
Yeah.

238
00:14:49,689 --> 00:14:52,656
Well... never know.

239
00:14:52,725 --> 00:14:53,725
You know?

240
00:15:04,404 --> 00:15:08,706
So, uh, you were
the one who, uh,

241
00:15:08,775 --> 00:15:10,219
found Father
Fitzgerald that night.

242
00:15:10,243 --> 00:15:11,509
That's right.

243
00:15:11,578 --> 00:15:14,812
Heard a bang, knew it
was a gunshot right away.

244
00:15:14,881 --> 00:15:16,626
Went running upstairs,
and there he was.

245
00:15:16,650 --> 00:15:19,583
There were other
people here that night?

246
00:15:19,653 --> 00:15:22,587
Father Burke, Sister
Katherine and Father Richards.

247
00:15:22,655 --> 00:15:24,634
They all came running
in just after I did.

248
00:15:24,658 --> 00:15:27,725
So you were present
when Father Fitzgerald,

249
00:15:27,794 --> 00:15:30,327
uh, spoke to Father
Richards, just before he died?

250
00:15:30,397 --> 00:15:31,562
Oh, yeah.

251
00:15:31,631 --> 00:15:33,831
Did you hear what he said?

252
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:34,999
No.

253
00:15:35,067 --> 00:15:36,846
He whispered in
Father Richards' ear.

254
00:15:36,870 --> 00:15:38,502
Oh.

255
00:15:38,571 --> 00:15:39,870
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

256
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:43,474
Well, did you, did you see
or hear anything unusual?

257
00:15:43,543 --> 00:15:46,410
I thought I heard
somebody running,

258
00:15:46,479 --> 00:15:48,111
but never saw who it was.

259
00:15:48,181 --> 00:15:50,114
No.

260
00:15:50,183 --> 00:15:51,861
Uh, anything else
out of the ordinary?

261
00:15:51,885 --> 00:15:54,919
Father Fitzgerald
was in the sanctuary

262
00:15:54,988 --> 00:15:57,488
about an hour or so
before he was shot.

263
00:15:57,556 --> 00:15:59,690
Somebody had taken
a crucifix off the wall

264
00:15:59,759 --> 00:16:01,839
and just smashed it
to pieces on the floor.

265
00:16:03,796 --> 00:16:07,632
And he was staring
down at what was left of it.

266
00:16:07,701 --> 00:16:11,335
Anyway, when I asked him
who did it, he just looked at me,

267
00:16:11,404 --> 00:16:13,004
turned around and marched off.

268
00:16:13,073 --> 00:16:16,007
It was like he knew who did it
and was gonna go after them.

269
00:16:16,076 --> 00:16:17,475
Did he say who it was?

270
00:16:17,544 --> 00:16:18,743
No.

271
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:21,144
Just wrote it down in
that black notebook of his.

272
00:16:21,214 --> 00:16:23,547
What black notebook?

273
00:16:23,616 --> 00:16:25,394
Last couple of months,
he took to carrying

274
00:16:25,418 --> 00:16:27,851
this black notebook around.

275
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:30,232
Every time you looked, he
was writing something down in it.

276
00:16:30,256 --> 00:16:33,124
Yeah? Did you see what
he was writing down?

277
00:16:33,193 --> 00:16:35,993
Never let anybody near it.

278
00:16:36,062 --> 00:16:38,829
That book wasn't
in the police report.

279
00:16:38,898 --> 00:16:41,832
It might still be around
here somewhere.

280
00:16:46,472 --> 00:16:48,406
Yeah, bet I know where it is.

281
00:16:53,413 --> 00:16:56,113
Daggone.

282
00:17:00,519 --> 00:17:03,687
Father Fitzgerald had me
fix the light in here once.

283
00:17:03,756 --> 00:17:06,924
Asked me to keep
this place secret.

284
00:17:06,993 --> 00:17:09,793
He wouldn't mind me telling
about it now, do you think?

285
00:17:09,863 --> 00:17:11,662
Oh, no, no.

286
00:17:11,731 --> 00:17:13,197
I think you may have

287
00:17:13,266 --> 00:17:15,826
just done him a big favor.

288
00:17:26,346 --> 00:17:27,644
I-I didn't mean to startle you.

289
00:17:27,714 --> 00:17:30,347
Well, you certainly did.

290
00:17:36,756 --> 00:17:39,101
You must be Doris Curtis.

291
00:17:39,125 --> 00:17:41,358
You're right; I have no choice.

292
00:17:41,427 --> 00:17:42,660
Who must you be?

293
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:46,597
I'm Alex Winthrop.

294
00:17:46,666 --> 00:17:47,931
I'm Nathan Carlino's lawyer.

295
00:17:48,001 --> 00:17:49,600
Get out of my kitchen.

296
00:17:49,669 --> 00:17:52,203
I have to talk to
you, Mrs. Curtis.

297
00:17:52,272 --> 00:17:54,238
I already told the police.

298
00:17:54,307 --> 00:17:56,006
I don't have to tell you.

299
00:17:56,076 --> 00:17:57,374
Actually, you do.

300
00:17:57,443 --> 00:17:58,743
If not here, then in court.

301
00:18:00,413 --> 00:18:04,348
You're not gonna trick
me into changing my story.

302
00:18:04,417 --> 00:18:06,250
I saw what I saw.

303
00:18:06,319 --> 00:18:10,154
You're sure it was Nathan
Carlino you saw running away?

304
00:18:10,223 --> 00:18:11,254
That's right.

305
00:18:11,324 --> 00:18:13,123
This window?

306
00:18:13,193 --> 00:18:14,758
No, that window.

307
00:18:18,964 --> 00:18:20,898
Sure looks bad
for Nathan Carlino.

308
00:18:22,968 --> 00:18:24,946
I guess it must have
come as quite a shock

309
00:18:24,970 --> 00:18:26,303
that he would do such a thing.

310
00:18:26,372 --> 00:18:28,105
No shock to me.

311
00:18:28,174 --> 00:18:29,506
I know his type.

312
00:18:29,575 --> 00:18:32,176
We dealt with a lot of his
people back where I come from.

313
00:18:32,245 --> 00:18:33,255
I could tell you plenty.

314
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:35,312
I bet you could.

315
00:18:35,381 --> 00:18:37,159
No, thank you. Uh, I'll just...

316
00:18:37,183 --> 00:18:38,816
take one for later.

317
00:18:39,919 --> 00:18:43,814
I-I'll take one for
my-my partner Ben.

318
00:18:43,856 --> 00:18:44,867
Thank you.

319
00:18:44,891 --> 00:18:47,091
Thank you.

320
00:18:50,697 --> 00:18:54,298
No, Kathy, please, trust
my judgment this time.

321
00:18:54,366 --> 00:18:56,311
It's not what you said.

322
00:18:56,335 --> 00:18:59,136
We can't do it now, after what
just happened to Father, no!

323
00:18:59,205 --> 00:19:00,348
Why? Why not... No!

324
00:19:00,372 --> 00:19:01,405
The timing is horrible!

325
00:19:01,473 --> 00:19:03,251
No! It's 4:00. We're late.

326
00:19:03,275 --> 00:19:04,374
We're not late.

327
00:19:04,443 --> 00:19:06,310
We have to wait.
The timing is...

328
00:19:07,547 --> 00:19:09,914
Sorry.

329
00:19:09,983 --> 00:19:13,017
You might try knocking first.

330
00:19:13,085 --> 00:19:15,645
Uh, yes, well, I was,
uh, going to do that,

331
00:19:15,688 --> 00:19:19,802
but, uh, I, um... I'm
looking for somebody.

332
00:19:19,826 --> 00:19:22,159
I'm Alex Winthrop.

333
00:19:22,227 --> 00:19:25,562
Um, I'm representing
Nathan Carlino.

334
00:19:25,632 --> 00:19:27,331
We have nothing to say to you.

335
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:30,634
Yeah, well, that seems
to be the general idea.

336
00:19:30,703 --> 00:19:32,303
Uh, you are...?

337
00:19:32,372 --> 00:19:34,404
This is Sister Katherine,

338
00:19:34,474 --> 00:19:36,206
and I'm Father Burke.

339
00:19:36,276 --> 00:19:37,441
Hi.

340
00:19:37,509 --> 00:19:40,010
Uh, you wouldn't mind
answering a couple of...

341
00:19:40,079 --> 00:19:41,245
Absolutely not.

342
00:19:41,314 --> 00:19:42,680
Not without a subpoena.

343
00:19:42,749 --> 00:19:44,215
Of course.

344
00:19:44,283 --> 00:19:48,219
Um... thanks, anyway.

345
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:51,855
Good-bye.

346
00:19:51,925 --> 00:19:55,926
Well, I can't thank you
enough for your help, Mr. Bell.

347
00:19:57,429 --> 00:19:59,330
Morning, Father Richards.

348
00:20:00,433 --> 00:20:01,599
Morning.

349
00:20:01,667 --> 00:20:02,800
You startled me.

350
00:20:02,869 --> 00:20:04,167
I-I didn't think...

351
00:20:05,772 --> 00:20:07,704
anybody would be in here.

352
00:20:07,774 --> 00:20:09,073
Father Paul Richards?

353
00:20:09,142 --> 00:20:11,408
Hi. Uh, I'm Ben Matlock,

354
00:20:11,477 --> 00:20:12,944
one of Nathan Carlino's lawyers.

355
00:20:13,012 --> 00:20:14,723
I wonder if I might... I'm...

356
00:20:14,747 --> 00:20:16,558
afraid I'm a little
busy right now.

357
00:20:16,582 --> 00:20:19,082
Things are chaotic around
here, as you can imagine.

358
00:20:19,152 --> 00:20:20,551
Oh, sure.

359
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:21,785
Excuse me.

360
00:20:21,854 --> 00:20:23,587
If-If... If you want to...

361
00:20:23,656 --> 00:20:26,490
uh, uh, do anything
in here, we're done.

362
00:20:26,559 --> 00:20:28,025
No. That's all right.

363
00:20:28,094 --> 00:20:31,995
I just remembered,
uh, what I was after

364
00:20:32,065 --> 00:20:34,065
Father Fitzgerald
kept someplace else.

365
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,399
Okay.

366
00:20:37,803 --> 00:20:39,736
Mr. Bell.

367
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,773
How are we doing?

368
00:20:44,777 --> 00:20:46,944
I'm not sure.

369
00:20:51,283 --> 00:20:53,017
How about that?

370
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:55,430
Are you at the
bottom of the page?

371
00:20:55,454 --> 00:20:56,953
Not yet.

372
00:20:57,023 --> 00:20:58,188
Criminy.

373
00:20:58,257 --> 00:20:59,456
Yeah.

374
00:20:59,525 --> 00:21:02,359
Boy, there was a lot going on

375
00:21:02,428 --> 00:21:03,994
out at St. Ignatius.

376
00:21:04,063 --> 00:21:06,863
Do you think all
this stuff is true?

377
00:21:06,932 --> 00:21:08,332
The man was a priest.

378
00:21:09,835 --> 00:21:11,001
You know, I think

379
00:21:11,070 --> 00:21:12,936
Father Fitzgerald was
right about one thing.

380
00:21:13,005 --> 00:21:15,272
Sister Katherine and Father
Burke are hiding something.

381
00:21:15,341 --> 00:21:17,674
Hmm.

382
00:21:17,743 --> 00:21:21,311
Maybe Tyler will
find out what it is.

383
00:21:21,380 --> 00:21:22,613
Hmm.

384
00:21:59,952 --> 00:22:00,884
Hey, man!

385
00:22:00,953 --> 00:22:02,453
Hey!

386
00:22:11,096 --> 00:22:13,163
Hey... that guy was playin' us!

387
00:22:29,315 --> 00:22:30,592
Why are you following me?

388
00:22:30,616 --> 00:22:31,915
I'm not following you!

389
00:22:31,984 --> 00:22:33,783
I mean... I was following you,

390
00:22:33,852 --> 00:22:36,220
but only because I thought
you were David Burke.

391
00:22:36,288 --> 00:22:37,554
<i>Father</i> David Burke.

392
00:22:37,623 --> 00:22:38,955
I<i> am</i> Father Burke.

393
00:22:39,024 --> 00:22:40,357
You can't be Father Burke.

394
00:22:40,426 --> 00:22:41,703
Why not?

395
00:22:41,727 --> 00:22:43,660
Because you're strangling me.

396
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:49,511
Sorry.

397
00:22:49,535 --> 00:22:50,612
It's a tough neighborhood.

398
00:22:50,636 --> 00:22:51,868
Yeah.

399
00:22:51,938 --> 00:22:53,978
People get hurt
around here all the time.

400
00:22:54,006 --> 00:22:55,639
Yeah.

401
00:22:55,708 --> 00:22:58,241
Practically every day.

402
00:22:58,311 --> 00:22:59,677
Yeah.

403
00:23:22,101 --> 00:23:26,904
He was like a father
to me, Mr. Matlock.

404
00:23:26,973 --> 00:23:30,340
He was also
devoted to this parish.

405
00:23:30,409 --> 00:23:33,811
I don't know how
we'll replace him.

406
00:23:33,879 --> 00:23:38,248
Evidently, he thought
you'd like to try.

407
00:23:43,755 --> 00:23:45,689
He was wrong about that.

408
00:23:45,757 --> 00:23:48,003
Well, you did take over.

409
00:23:48,027 --> 00:23:51,428
Only temporarily, until the
archbishop makes a decision.

410
00:23:51,496 --> 00:23:54,364
Look, I know Father Fitzgerald
thought I was ambitious.

411
00:23:54,433 --> 00:23:56,834
He said it to my face.

412
00:23:56,902 --> 00:23:59,736
It's simply not true.

413
00:24:01,841 --> 00:24:07,812
Uh... that's not the
half of it, Father.

414
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:08,890
What do you mean?

415
00:24:08,914 --> 00:24:11,581
Well, in his notes

416
00:24:11,650 --> 00:24:14,451
in his little black book,

417
00:24:14,520 --> 00:24:17,721
Father Fitzgerald said that...

418
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:20,190
you probably wanted his job

419
00:24:20,259 --> 00:24:22,893
to make it easier for you to...

420
00:24:22,962 --> 00:24:24,661
dip into church funds.

421
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:30,567
He thought I was stealing.

422
00:24:30,636 --> 00:24:33,403
Yes, and investing
in the stock market.

423
00:24:33,473 --> 00:24:35,338
It's not true.

424
00:24:35,408 --> 00:24:37,006
Why'd he write it down?

425
00:24:37,076 --> 00:24:41,611
Look, Sister Katherine
does the books.

426
00:24:41,680 --> 00:24:43,947
Ask her if anything's missing.

427
00:24:44,016 --> 00:24:45,949
She should be in around 9:00.

428
00:24:55,761 --> 00:24:59,997
No, nothing unusual about
anything so far, Mr. Winthrop.

429
00:25:00,066 --> 00:25:01,376
You're a whiz.

430
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:02,610
Now, where did you
learn accounting?

431
00:25:02,634 --> 00:25:03,667
Oh, I took

432
00:25:03,736 --> 00:25:05,514
some courses over
at community college.

433
00:25:05,538 --> 00:25:07,103
Father Fitzgerald's idea.

434
00:25:07,173 --> 00:25:10,774
He needed a bookkeeper,
and my order volunteered me.

435
00:25:10,843 --> 00:25:12,754
I didn't know a
credit from a debit,

436
00:25:12,778 --> 00:25:15,713
but Father Fitzgerald
had faith I'd learn.

437
00:25:15,781 --> 00:25:19,883
I, um, I understand you were
here the night he was murdered.

438
00:25:19,952 --> 00:25:22,219
Uh, I was getting
everything in order

439
00:25:22,288 --> 00:25:24,254
for our annual diocesan audit.

440
00:25:24,323 --> 00:25:26,883
Want some coffee, Kat...?

441
00:25:29,628 --> 00:25:32,062
Good to see you again.

442
00:25:33,599 --> 00:25:35,566
That's some handshake.

443
00:25:35,634 --> 00:25:37,434
Tyler told me you were strong.

444
00:25:37,503 --> 00:25:39,069
Tyler...

445
00:25:39,138 --> 00:25:42,272
Oh, you mean the gentleman
who's been following me.

446
00:25:42,341 --> 00:25:44,441
He's an associate of mine.

447
00:25:44,510 --> 00:25:47,055
Why follow me, of all people?

448
00:25:47,079 --> 00:25:50,747
Well, because of what
Father Fitzgerald wrote in this.

449
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:58,121
"Ignoring the parish,
his duties, and the church

450
00:25:58,190 --> 00:26:02,125
"to carry on in a sinful and
scandalous manner with...

451
00:26:02,194 --> 00:26:04,361
Sister Katherine."

452
00:26:04,429 --> 00:26:05,429
That's a lie.

453
00:26:05,464 --> 00:26:07,397
Father...

454
00:26:09,302 --> 00:26:10,400
Don't.

455
00:26:10,469 --> 00:26:12,869
The only scandal at
St. Ignatius existed

456
00:26:12,938 --> 00:26:15,339
in Father Fitzgerald's mind.

457
00:26:20,446 --> 00:26:23,613
There are no irregularities
in our books, Mr. Winthrop.

458
00:26:23,682 --> 00:26:27,217
If you'll excuse me, I'd
like to get back to work.

459
00:26:36,495 --> 00:26:38,428
Okay.

460
00:26:40,665 --> 00:26:42,599
So what's the plan?

461
00:26:42,667 --> 00:26:46,103
Well, uh, first court
and then lunch.

462
00:26:46,171 --> 00:26:49,172
I don't mean the
plan for your day.

463
00:26:49,241 --> 00:26:51,319
I mean the plan for my case.

464
00:26:51,343 --> 00:26:54,311
Oh, I... I hope to
prove you're innocent.

465
00:26:54,380 --> 00:26:55,790
How are you going to do it?

466
00:26:55,814 --> 00:26:56,746
You got suspects?

467
00:26:56,815 --> 00:26:57,747
We're working on it.

468
00:26:57,816 --> 00:26:58,748
Well, come on, shoot.

469
00:26:58,817 --> 00:27:00,250
Who are they?

470
00:27:00,319 --> 00:27:02,852
I don't think this is
the time to talk about it.

471
00:27:02,921 --> 00:27:05,233
How come you're,
uh, holding out on me?

472
00:27:05,257 --> 00:27:06,923
Who are these people?

473
00:27:06,992 --> 00:27:09,393
I have people of my own
who could help check 'em out.

474
00:27:09,462 --> 00:27:10,727
No.

475
00:27:10,796 --> 00:27:13,363
A maniac priest killer
is on the loose out there;

476
00:27:13,432 --> 00:27:15,432
a maniac who could
prove me innocent.

477
00:27:15,501 --> 00:27:17,434
Who are these damn suspects?

478
00:27:18,537 --> 00:27:21,304
Two priests and a nun.

479
00:27:22,407 --> 00:27:24,541
Two priests and a nun?

480
00:27:24,609 --> 00:27:25,676
Yeah.

481
00:27:25,745 --> 00:27:27,411
I'm a dead man.

482
00:27:31,250 --> 00:27:33,850
And the next thing
I hear is Mr. Bell,

483
00:27:33,919 --> 00:27:36,920
hollering from the other
room, for me to call the police.

484
00:27:36,988 --> 00:27:39,756
So I go to the phone,
and that's when I saw him.

485
00:27:39,825 --> 00:27:41,369
Who did you see, Mrs. Curtis?

486
00:27:41,393 --> 00:27:42,325
Him.

487
00:27:42,395 --> 00:27:44,928
Nathan Carlino, him.

488
00:27:44,997 --> 00:27:47,530
I know it was him 'cause I
saw his picture in the paper.

489
00:27:47,599 --> 00:27:48,844
Let the record show

490
00:27:48,868 --> 00:27:52,236
that the witness pointed to
the defendant Nathan Carlino.

491
00:27:52,304 --> 00:27:56,372
Now, Mrs. Curtis, could
you see Mr. Carlino clearly?

492
00:27:56,442 --> 00:27:58,420
He wasn't more than
ten feet from the window

493
00:27:58,444 --> 00:27:59,810
when he ran past.

494
00:27:59,879 --> 00:28:01,311
But it was 11:00 at night.

495
00:28:01,380 --> 00:28:03,112
Ho-How could you see his face?

496
00:28:03,182 --> 00:28:07,217
They keep a big light on
in the yard, all night long,

497
00:28:07,286 --> 00:28:08,852
near the window.

498
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:11,088
I saw his face
clearly, believe me.

499
00:28:11,156 --> 00:28:13,089
Oh, I do, Mrs. Curtis.

500
00:28:13,158 --> 00:28:14,658
No more questions, Your Honor.

501
00:28:14,727 --> 00:28:17,828
Cross-examine, Mr. Matlock?

502
00:28:18,931 --> 00:28:22,966
Uh, Mrs. Curtis, uh,

503
00:28:23,035 --> 00:28:26,770
how long have you
worked at the rectory

504
00:28:26,839 --> 00:28:29,272
out at St. Ignatius?

505
00:28:29,341 --> 00:28:30,941
33 years.

506
00:28:31,009 --> 00:28:32,242
Well, that's a long time.

507
00:28:32,311 --> 00:28:34,944
And how long had you
known Father Fitzgerald?

508
00:28:35,014 --> 00:28:36,579
He was the one that hired me.

509
00:28:36,648 --> 00:28:39,849
Oh... 33 years.

510
00:28:39,918 --> 00:28:42,519
So I guess you were
pretty fond of him.

511
00:28:42,588 --> 00:28:45,589
Oh, that man was a saint.

512
00:28:45,657 --> 00:28:47,958
How can you not
be fond of a saint?

513
00:28:48,027 --> 00:28:52,462
About, about how far do
you live from the rectory?

514
00:28:52,531 --> 00:28:55,332
Oh, about a 20-minute drive.

515
00:28:55,401 --> 00:28:57,600
Oh, you drive to work?

516
00:28:57,670 --> 00:29:00,370
Well, I'd have to transfer
twice if I took the bus.

517
00:29:00,439 --> 00:29:03,474
Besides, I need my
car to buy groceries.

518
00:29:03,542 --> 00:29:05,342
Oh... oh, oh.

519
00:29:05,411 --> 00:29:08,545
So part of your job
is grocery shopping?

520
00:29:08,614 --> 00:29:11,581
Do you ever see a
priest in a checkout line?

521
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:18,655
What I'm getting at is that
if you were unable to drive,

522
00:29:18,724 --> 00:29:22,559
uh, you might lose
your job, mightn't you?

523
00:29:22,628 --> 00:29:24,094
Probably.

524
00:29:24,163 --> 00:29:27,030
Well, Mrs. Curtis, have,
uh, have you gotten

525
00:29:27,099 --> 00:29:30,233
any traffic tickets
for moving violations

526
00:29:30,302 --> 00:29:32,469
in the last, oh, year or so?

527
00:29:33,739 --> 00:29:34,804
Yes.

528
00:29:34,874 --> 00:29:36,006
How many?

529
00:29:36,075 --> 00:29:38,141
Well, I don't remember.
Let me see if I can

530
00:29:38,210 --> 00:29:39,221
help you out on that.

531
00:29:39,245 --> 00:29:43,647
Um... see here...

532
00:29:43,715 --> 00:29:46,816
you received one
for running a stop sign

533
00:29:46,885 --> 00:29:49,119
and one for not
stopping at a crosswalk

534
00:29:49,188 --> 00:29:50,387
when someone was in it,

535
00:29:50,456 --> 00:29:52,822
and one for a
minor fender bender.

536
00:29:52,892 --> 00:29:55,859
Now, that's so many
that you get another,

537
00:29:55,928 --> 00:29:57,593
they'll suspend your license.

538
00:29:57,662 --> 00:29:59,095
Is that correct?

539
00:30:00,198 --> 00:30:02,265
Yes.

540
00:30:02,334 --> 00:30:06,069
Why have you gotten so
many traffic tickets lately?

541
00:30:06,138 --> 00:30:08,638
I don't know.

542
00:30:08,707 --> 00:30:10,873
Um, the newspaper

543
00:30:10,942 --> 00:30:15,178
that you saw
Mr. Carlino's picture in...

544
00:30:15,247 --> 00:30:17,581
Is it the<i> Atlanta Examiner?</i>

545
00:30:17,649 --> 00:30:18,582
Yes.

546
00:30:18,650 --> 00:30:21,484
You subscribe to
that paper? Yes.

547
00:30:21,554 --> 00:30:26,423
And you get the large
print edition, don't you?

548
00:30:27,526 --> 00:30:29,592
Yes.

549
00:30:29,662 --> 00:30:31,339
Why, why do you
get the large print

550
00:30:31,363 --> 00:30:33,923
instead of the regular edition?

551
00:30:34,867 --> 00:30:37,300
Because... You don't see

552
00:30:37,369 --> 00:30:39,769
so good anymore, do you?

553
00:30:39,839 --> 00:30:41,238
And that might explain

554
00:30:41,307 --> 00:30:44,508
why you've gotten
so many traffic tickets.

555
00:30:44,577 --> 00:30:48,745
It might explain why
you never allow anyone

556
00:30:48,814 --> 00:30:51,815
at the rectory to
see your newspaper.

557
00:30:51,884 --> 00:30:54,885
You don't want
anyone at St. Ignatius

558
00:30:54,953 --> 00:30:56,731
to know you're
losing your eyesight

559
00:30:56,755 --> 00:31:00,790
and in danger of losing
your driver's license,

560
00:31:00,860 --> 00:31:03,660
'cause that could mean
the loss of your job.

561
00:31:03,728 --> 00:31:06,329
Couldn't it?

562
00:31:06,398 --> 00:31:07,530
Yes.

563
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:12,435
You were so very fond
of Father Fitzgerald,

564
00:31:12,504 --> 00:31:15,538
you wanted to see
his killer punished,

565
00:31:15,608 --> 00:31:18,141
and so you told the police

566
00:31:18,210 --> 00:31:22,212
that that night you
saw Nathan Carlino.

567
00:31:22,280 --> 00:31:26,850
Did you, in fact, see
Nathan Carlino that night?

568
00:31:30,322 --> 00:31:33,156
No.

569
00:31:33,225 --> 00:31:36,859
Did you see anyone running away

570
00:31:36,928 --> 00:31:38,995
from the rectory that night?

571
00:31:39,064 --> 00:31:41,130
No.

572
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:43,500
Thank you for your honesty.

573
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:50,240
I happen to know

574
00:31:50,309 --> 00:31:54,311
that Father Fitzgerald
was very fond of you, too.

575
00:31:54,379 --> 00:31:57,214
You're the only one he
had good things to say about

576
00:31:57,282 --> 00:31:59,715
in the last days of his life.

577
00:31:59,785 --> 00:32:02,919
It was probably the cookies.

578
00:32:05,023 --> 00:32:07,424
No further questions.

579
00:32:16,168 --> 00:32:18,368
Father Burke.

580
00:32:18,436 --> 00:32:20,581
I need to talk to you.

581
00:32:20,605 --> 00:32:22,839
I'm hearing confession
in five minutes.

582
00:32:22,908 --> 00:32:24,485
I'm trying to find
Sister Katherine.

583
00:32:24,509 --> 00:32:25,509
I haven't seen her.

584
00:32:25,544 --> 00:32:26,476
That's the problem.

585
00:32:26,544 --> 00:32:27,643
Nobody has.

586
00:32:27,712 --> 00:32:29,457
I tried her convent,
I tried the hospital.

587
00:32:29,481 --> 00:32:30,847
No one knows where she is.

588
00:32:30,916 --> 00:32:32,860
Sister Katherine might
be here later today.

589
00:32:32,884 --> 00:32:33,884
Is this urgent?

590
00:32:35,921 --> 00:32:38,621
Father, Sister
Katherine was involved

591
00:32:38,690 --> 00:32:40,790
in the Carlino case after all.

592
00:32:40,859 --> 00:32:42,893
That's absurd.

593
00:32:42,962 --> 00:32:43,962
I need to find her.

594
00:32:43,995 --> 00:32:45,540
Do you have any
idea where she is?

595
00:32:45,564 --> 00:32:48,231
I'm sorry, no.

596
00:32:48,300 --> 00:32:49,766
Thanks for your time.

597
00:32:49,834 --> 00:32:53,637
If you hear from her,
have her give me a call.

598
00:33:17,729 --> 00:33:21,569
Got another sexy girl for
you in about 15 minutes!

599
00:33:25,136 --> 00:33:28,976
Yeah, he's bringing
her around back!

600
00:33:30,809 --> 00:33:33,410
See that man following
me real close back there?

601
00:33:33,479 --> 00:33:34,889
Make sure he
doesn't get too far.

602
00:33:34,913 --> 00:33:36,257
James Brown. Okay?

603
00:33:36,281 --> 00:33:38,482
Yeah. All right, man.

604
00:33:44,056 --> 00:33:46,255
Yeah, that's right, Jack.

605
00:33:48,259 --> 00:33:50,338
What's goin' on,
brother? I like your shoes.

606
00:33:50,362 --> 00:33:51,795
So do I. Excuse me.

607
00:33:56,602 --> 00:33:58,068
Check out them socks, homie.

608
00:33:58,137 --> 00:33:59,536
Hey, I'm warning you.

609
00:33:59,605 --> 00:34:02,017
How do you think those
pants'd look on me, C.J.?

610
00:34:02,041 --> 00:34:04,040
I will get even
with you for this!

611
00:34:04,109 --> 00:34:05,408
Get off of me!

612
00:34:38,710 --> 00:34:42,312
♪ ♪

613
00:34:48,219 --> 00:34:49,652
Mr. Winthrop.

614
00:34:49,721 --> 00:34:50,832
I've been expecting you.

615
00:34:50,856 --> 00:34:52,188
Come in.

616
00:34:52,257 --> 00:34:54,156
Thank you.

617
00:34:54,225 --> 00:34:56,025
You tricked me.

618
00:34:57,662 --> 00:34:58,702
That's right, I did.

619
00:34:58,730 --> 00:35:00,375
I... I thought that
you could lead me

620
00:35:00,399 --> 00:35:02,042
to Sister Katherine
and that I...

621
00:35:02,066 --> 00:35:04,834
I'd catch you two
doing something... uh...

622
00:35:06,271 --> 00:35:08,805
uh... incriminating.

623
00:35:10,475 --> 00:35:11,774
What<i> are</i> you doing?

624
00:35:11,844 --> 00:35:13,510
None of your business.

625
00:35:13,579 --> 00:35:14,944
David, please.

626
00:35:15,013 --> 00:35:17,013
He has no right
spying on you, Katie.

627
00:35:17,082 --> 00:35:20,083
He's only trying to find out
who killed Father Fitzgerald.

628
00:35:20,152 --> 00:35:22,418
Whose apartment is this? Mine.

629
00:35:22,488 --> 00:35:24,787
Don't nuns usually
live in convents?

630
00:35:24,857 --> 00:35:26,823
Yes, they do.

631
00:35:26,891 --> 00:35:28,424
I'm going to tell him, David.

632
00:35:33,465 --> 00:35:34,964
I'm on leave from the convent.

633
00:35:35,032 --> 00:35:37,467
I've applied for
release from my vows.

634
00:35:37,535 --> 00:35:39,575
In a few weeks, I'll
no longer be a nun.

635
00:35:40,639 --> 00:35:41,704
That's serious.

636
00:35:41,773 --> 00:35:43,117
Did Father Fitzgerald
know about that?

637
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:44,141
No.

638
00:35:44,209 --> 00:35:45,209
I kept it from him.

639
00:35:45,243 --> 00:35:47,277
Not because I
wanted to deceive him,

640
00:35:47,345 --> 00:35:49,345
but to spare his feelings.

641
00:35:49,414 --> 00:35:51,681
Father Fitzgerald thought
of me as a daughter

642
00:35:51,749 --> 00:35:53,883
and would have wanted
to change my mind.

643
00:35:54,986 --> 00:35:57,753
Besides, my decision to leave

644
00:35:57,822 --> 00:36:00,623
involves another person,
and I couldn't reveal that.

645
00:36:00,692 --> 00:36:02,425
You're the other person.

646
00:36:07,532 --> 00:36:09,666
I love Katie.

647
00:36:09,734 --> 00:36:11,233
I'm leaving the priesthood.

648
00:36:13,438 --> 00:36:15,171
So Father Fitzgerald was right

649
00:36:15,240 --> 00:36:16,384
about you two. No!

650
00:36:17,976 --> 00:36:20,209
He accused us of
breaking our vows.

651
00:36:20,278 --> 00:36:21,711
We haven't done that.

652
00:36:21,780 --> 00:36:24,080
Well... what would have happened

653
00:36:24,148 --> 00:36:26,916
if he told your superiors that
you were having an affair?

654
00:36:26,984 --> 00:36:28,997
We haven't broken our vows.

655
00:36:29,021 --> 00:36:31,654
Ours is a moral dilemma
between ourselves.

656
00:36:31,723 --> 00:36:33,390
We simply love each other.

657
00:36:33,458 --> 00:36:34,757
It's not a motive

658
00:36:34,826 --> 00:36:37,386
for murdering dear
Father Fitzgerald.

659
00:36:40,499 --> 00:36:44,434
Looks like Father
Fitzgerald was wrong again.

660
00:36:44,503 --> 00:36:47,270
I'm really sorry
that I bothered you.

661
00:36:49,474 --> 00:36:51,541
I'll see you later.

662
00:36:51,609 --> 00:36:53,743
Good luck.

663
00:37:04,789 --> 00:37:06,689
Sister Katherine
and Father Burke

664
00:37:06,758 --> 00:37:08,758
don't have a motive.

665
00:37:12,697 --> 00:37:14,275
Neither does our client.

666
00:37:14,299 --> 00:37:16,466
Neither does Father Richards.

667
00:37:16,534 --> 00:37:18,768
Father Fitzgerald was
wrong about all of them.

668
00:37:18,836 --> 00:37:20,202
I don't get it.

669
00:37:20,272 --> 00:37:21,571
What was going on with him?

670
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:24,240
Why did he think all those
people were up to no good?

671
00:37:26,378 --> 00:37:28,010
I don't know.

672
00:37:28,080 --> 00:37:30,914
You know... as
far as I can tell,

673
00:37:30,982 --> 00:37:33,483
no one had a motive
to commit this murder.

674
00:37:36,555 --> 00:37:38,788
You're right.

675
00:37:40,392 --> 00:37:42,492
No one had a motive.

676
00:37:53,972 --> 00:37:58,441
Father Richards, how
would you describe

677
00:37:58,510 --> 00:38:02,545
your relationship
with Father Fitzgerald?

678
00:38:04,683 --> 00:38:07,283
He was my teacher.

679
00:38:07,352 --> 00:38:09,619
My mentor.

680
00:38:09,688 --> 00:38:11,454
My friend.

681
00:38:12,924 --> 00:38:15,658
And those are
terms of affection.

682
00:38:15,727 --> 00:38:18,628
I admired and respected
Father Fitzgerald

683
00:38:18,697 --> 00:38:20,930
like I have no
other human being.

684
00:38:20,999 --> 00:38:24,500
Was that admiration
and respect mutual?

685
00:38:26,237 --> 00:38:28,137
I like to think that it was.

686
00:38:29,974 --> 00:38:32,141
Uh, Father Richards, uh,

687
00:38:32,210 --> 00:38:35,010
are you aware that
Father Fitzgerald

688
00:38:35,079 --> 00:38:38,814
carried a little black
book around with him

689
00:38:38,883 --> 00:38:40,950
in which he wrote, oh,

690
00:38:41,018 --> 00:38:43,620
various thoughts
and facts and...?

691
00:38:44,723 --> 00:38:46,043
Everybody knew that. Uh-huh.

692
00:38:47,125 --> 00:38:48,791
Well...

693
00:38:48,860 --> 00:38:54,196
in his book... he
characterized you

694
00:38:54,265 --> 00:38:59,102
as "a selfish,
status-seeking manipulator."

695
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:00,603
Were you aware of that?

696
00:39:00,672 --> 00:39:03,839
I haven't seen his book, but...

697
00:39:03,908 --> 00:39:05,874
he said worse
than that to my face.

698
00:39:05,944 --> 00:39:07,643
Oh?

699
00:39:07,712 --> 00:39:10,646
Uh, were you aware

700
00:39:10,715 --> 00:39:14,683
that he told the
archbishop the same?

701
00:39:16,220 --> 00:39:18,020
No, I was not.

702
00:39:19,490 --> 00:39:23,158
Well, why would he say
such things about you?

703
00:39:25,296 --> 00:39:26,762
I don't know.

704
00:39:26,832 --> 00:39:29,198
Well, you... you
and Father Fitzgerald

705
00:39:29,267 --> 00:39:32,134
had known one
another for many years.

706
00:39:32,203 --> 00:39:34,870
He was your friend, your mentor.

707
00:39:34,939 --> 00:39:39,908
Didn't this name-calling seem
a bizarre behavior for him?

708
00:39:41,012 --> 00:39:42,012
I suppose.

709
00:39:42,047 --> 00:39:43,579
And he accused you

710
00:39:43,648 --> 00:39:45,258
of stealing money
from the church,

711
00:39:45,282 --> 00:39:49,919
an accusation that we both
know is totally unfounded.

712
00:39:49,988 --> 00:39:52,188
Didn't that seem a bit bizarre?

713
00:39:52,257 --> 00:39:53,856
Yes.

714
00:39:53,925 --> 00:39:56,493
And when he... when
he jumped up at the...

715
00:39:56,561 --> 00:40:01,364
the ribbon-cutting ceremony
at-at St. Ignatius and...

716
00:40:01,433 --> 00:40:03,077
and disrupted the
whole ceremony,

717
00:40:03,101 --> 00:40:05,602
didn't that seem
a... a bit bizarre?

718
00:40:06,704 --> 00:40:08,103
Yes. So, in...

719
00:40:08,173 --> 00:40:10,873
in spite of these
false accusations

720
00:40:10,941 --> 00:40:14,977
and bizarre behavior,
you still remained friends?

721
00:40:17,081 --> 00:40:18,347
Yes, we did.

722
00:40:19,451 --> 00:40:22,919
Father Richards, um...

723
00:40:22,987 --> 00:40:26,522
could that be because...

724
00:40:26,591 --> 00:40:31,093
you had a suspicion of why
he was acting so strangely?

725
00:40:34,499 --> 00:40:36,298
I can't answer that.

726
00:40:36,368 --> 00:40:38,534
Oh, I... I understand.

727
00:40:38,603 --> 00:40:42,905
Uh, who served as Father
Fitzgerald's confessor?

728
00:40:44,542 --> 00:40:46,042
I did.

729
00:40:46,111 --> 00:40:47,710
And you are bound

730
00:40:47,779 --> 00:40:51,213
by the confidentialities
of confession,

731
00:40:51,282 --> 00:40:53,783
even after his
death, aren't you?

732
00:40:53,852 --> 00:40:55,117
Yes, I am.

733
00:40:55,187 --> 00:40:57,331
And that's why you can't
answer my questions?

734
00:40:57,355 --> 00:40:58,355
Yes.

735
00:40:58,390 --> 00:41:00,234
Uh, that being the
case, Your Honor,

736
00:41:00,258 --> 00:41:02,325
as stipulated in chambers,

737
00:41:02,393 --> 00:41:06,729
I would like to
introduce into evidence

738
00:41:06,797 --> 00:41:10,900
Father Fitzgerald's
medical record

739
00:41:10,969 --> 00:41:13,369
from his physician.

740
00:41:13,437 --> 00:41:15,304
It states

741
00:41:15,373 --> 00:41:17,885
that Father Fitzgerald
was suffering

742
00:41:17,909 --> 00:41:20,476
from a malignant brain tumor,

743
00:41:20,545 --> 00:41:23,012
which was suspected to disrupt

744
00:41:23,081 --> 00:41:25,314
normal intellectual reasoning

745
00:41:25,383 --> 00:41:28,284
and alter personality behavior.

746
00:41:28,353 --> 00:41:30,431
The autopsy didn't show it

747
00:41:30,455 --> 00:41:33,323
because of the
location of the wound.

748
00:41:33,391 --> 00:41:35,559
Objection, Your Honor.

749
00:41:35,593 --> 00:41:37,126
Mr. Matlock is testifying.

750
00:41:37,195 --> 00:41:38,661
Sustained.

751
00:41:38,730 --> 00:41:40,863
I beg your pardon, Your Honor.

752
00:41:42,167 --> 00:41:48,571
Um... Father
Richards, did you, uh...

753
00:41:48,639 --> 00:41:51,774
or were you surprised

754
00:41:51,843 --> 00:41:54,577
when Father Fitzgerald

755
00:41:54,645 --> 00:41:58,647
jumped up and disrupted
the ribbon-cutting ceremony?

756
00:41:59,751 --> 00:42:00,683
No.

757
00:42:00,752 --> 00:42:01,951
Not particularly.

758
00:42:02,019 --> 00:42:03,786
You know what that means to me?

759
00:42:03,855 --> 00:42:07,957
That means that you knew

760
00:42:08,025 --> 00:42:12,094
of Father Fitzgerald's
medical condition.

761
00:42:14,032 --> 00:42:15,564
Oh, okay.

762
00:42:15,634 --> 00:42:18,868
Okay, I'm sorry.

763
00:42:18,937 --> 00:42:21,804
Where did Father
Fitzgerald go to college?

764
00:42:24,475 --> 00:42:26,108
Notre Dame.

765
00:42:26,177 --> 00:42:27,443
And he was pretty proud

766
00:42:27,512 --> 00:42:29,457
of that, too, wasn't
he? Yes, he was.

767
00:42:29,481 --> 00:42:32,114
And one of his
prized possessions

768
00:42:32,183 --> 00:42:35,618
was his Notre Dame
graduation ring, wasn't it?

769
00:42:35,687 --> 00:42:36,619
Yes.

770
00:42:36,688 --> 00:42:39,255
Okay, I want to show you

771
00:42:39,324 --> 00:42:42,525
a blowup of a photograph

772
00:42:42,594 --> 00:42:46,629
taken at the now famous
ribbon-cutting ceremony.

773
00:42:46,697 --> 00:42:48,131
Here.

774
00:42:48,199 --> 00:42:50,566
Uh, this is a blowup

775
00:42:50,635 --> 00:42:54,470
of a photograph of
Father Richards' hand

776
00:42:54,539 --> 00:42:57,206
on Father Fitzgerald's shoulder.

777
00:42:57,275 --> 00:42:58,407
You see that?

778
00:42:58,476 --> 00:42:59,875
Oh, see that?

779
00:43:00,979 --> 00:43:07,783
See, now... will
you tell us, please:

780
00:43:07,852 --> 00:43:10,752
what is that ring
on your finger?

781
00:43:13,658 --> 00:43:14,790
Right there.

782
00:43:14,859 --> 00:43:18,260
It's a, um...

783
00:43:18,329 --> 00:43:20,462
it's a Notre Dame
graduation ring.

784
00:43:20,532 --> 00:43:22,231
What are you doing with it?

785
00:43:23,335 --> 00:43:24,867
Father Fitzgerald gave it to me.

786
00:43:24,936 --> 00:43:30,072
Father Fitzgerald gave you one
of his most prized possessions

787
00:43:30,140 --> 00:43:31,741
because he loved you

788
00:43:31,810 --> 00:43:34,109
and he wanted you to have it

789
00:43:34,179 --> 00:43:37,013
in case anything
happened to him,

790
00:43:37,081 --> 00:43:38,413
didn't he?

791
00:43:38,483 --> 00:43:40,716
I really can't
answer that question.

792
00:43:40,785 --> 00:43:42,384
It's a confidence.

793
00:43:42,454 --> 00:43:44,320
Well, what about this, then?

794
00:43:45,423 --> 00:43:49,292
There's another
blowup of a hand.

795
00:43:49,360 --> 00:43:53,296
If Father Fitzgerald
gave you that ring,

796
00:43:53,365 --> 00:43:56,632
what is it doing on his finger

797
00:43:56,701 --> 00:43:59,701
after he was shot
to death in his office?

798
00:44:05,776 --> 00:44:09,178
Father, what do most
Catholics consider

799
00:44:09,247 --> 00:44:13,649
the worst sin, the
one unforgivable sin?

800
00:44:13,718 --> 00:44:15,351
Suicide.

801
00:44:15,420 --> 00:44:18,320
Suicide.

802
00:44:18,389 --> 00:44:22,524
The moment you heard that
shot, you knew what had happened.

803
00:44:22,594 --> 00:44:25,227
Isn't it true you ran down

804
00:44:25,296 --> 00:44:28,830
to Father Fitzgerald's
office and did two things?

805
00:44:29,934 --> 00:44:31,834
You put the gun in your pocket,

806
00:44:31,903 --> 00:44:34,637
and you put the ring
back on his finger,

807
00:44:34,705 --> 00:44:39,074
so that no one would ever
know he had given it to you,

808
00:44:39,143 --> 00:44:42,244
because he had been thinking

809
00:44:42,313 --> 00:44:47,483
about doing exactly
what he did do:

810
00:44:47,552 --> 00:44:50,218
taking his own life.

811
00:44:51,856 --> 00:44:54,223
It was suicide, wasn't it?

812
00:44:58,762 --> 00:44:59,762
Yes.

813
00:44:59,831 --> 00:45:01,263
Yes.

814
00:45:01,332 --> 00:45:04,366
And you slipped out of the room,

815
00:45:04,435 --> 00:45:06,995
disposed of the gun...

816
00:45:07,739 --> 00:45:11,039
which is why everyone
thought it was murder...

817
00:45:12,510 --> 00:45:16,178
and you came back into
the room after Mr. Bell,

818
00:45:16,247 --> 00:45:21,617
Sister Katherine and
Father Burke had arrived.

819
00:45:21,686 --> 00:45:23,852
Yes, I did.

820
00:45:23,922 --> 00:45:26,422
And Father Fitzgerald

821
00:45:26,490 --> 00:45:30,793
never accused Nathan Carlino.

822
00:45:30,861 --> 00:45:34,397
You did that...

823
00:45:34,465 --> 00:45:37,800
to spare your beloved friend

824
00:45:37,868 --> 00:45:41,670
the stigma of suicide.

825
00:45:41,740 --> 00:45:45,608
He gave up his seat in Heaven

826
00:45:45,676 --> 00:45:48,745
because he didn't want
to inflict any more damage

827
00:45:48,813 --> 00:45:52,815
on the church and the people
he spent his whole life serving.

828
00:45:57,521 --> 00:46:00,489
I couldn't let him
die in disgrace.

829
00:46:07,265 --> 00:46:09,932
It just wasn't right.

830
00:46:16,807 --> 00:46:23,746
Your Honor, in light
of these revelations,

831
00:46:23,814 --> 00:46:29,418
I move the charges against
my client be dismissed.

832
00:46:30,522 --> 00:46:32,287
Any objections?

833
00:46:32,357 --> 00:46:33,822
No, Your Honor.

834
00:46:33,892 --> 00:46:35,424
Case dismissed.

835
00:46:36,528 --> 00:46:39,088
This court is adjourned.

836
00:46:43,001 --> 00:46:44,834
Congratulations.

837
00:46:46,938 --> 00:46:49,498
This worked out all right.

838
00:46:51,075 --> 00:46:54,143
I wasn't co-counsel on this.

839
00:46:56,547 --> 00:46:58,915
I was counsel.

840
00:47:04,222 --> 00:47:06,289
Want a $20 hot dog?

841
00:47:08,426 --> 00:47:10,359
I want a case of 'em.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
